'''Chromastone''' is the [[Omnitrix]]'s DNA sample of a [[Crystalsapien (Classic)|Crystalsapien]]{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}} from the planet [[Petropia (Classic)|Petropia]].<ref name = Tetrax>[[Tetrax Shard (Classic)|Tetrax Shard]]</ref><ref name="TSoC"/>

==Appearance==
Chromastone is a humanoid silicon-based<ref name="IM">''[[Inside Man]]''</ref> alien made of extremely durable crystal. His body is overall indigo, with several dark lines and spots. His hands and face are magenta, and he also sports six magenta shards on his back, two on his chest, and one on the top of his head that resembles a horn. His face consists of a mouth and one large green eye at the center.

In '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', Chromastone wore the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original Omnitrix]]/[[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] on his chest.

In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Heroes United]]'', Chromastone had green teeth and some of his dark lines were missing.

In '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', Chromastone has two unique designs. The first, which appears in ''[[Trouble Helix]]'', looked mostly the same as in '''Alien Force''' and '''Ultimate Alien''' except that the crystals on his back and head were much longer. Much like before, the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]] symbol is on his chest.

The second design, which appeared in ''[[A New Dawn]]'', is drastically different. He has three additional crystal shards on each shoulder and forearm, one on each knee, and two on the sides of his head. The crystals on his chest and the four small shards on his back are gone. His neck is now longer, his face has a magenta chin that resembles a mouth guard, and he now speaks without moving his mouth at all. He also has indigo rock hands with five magenta crystalline fingers. He now wears a green jumpsuit with white stripes on the waist, green and white-striped bands on his wrists and thighs, and the Omnitrix symbol has been relocated to his right pectoral.

