*Chromastone has more abilities than the ones Ben is aware of.<ref name = Tetrax /><ref name="TSoC" /> However, they are largely unexplored.
*Regarding Chromastone's destruction and subsequent reformation/merging into [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]] in ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]'':
**It had nothing to do with Vilgax's sword being covered in crystal before he destroyed him.{{Refn|[[:File:AF Diamondhead Nothing to Do With Vilgax's Sword.PNG]]|group = DM}}
**Ben does not know the explanation behind Chromastone merging with Diamondhead, but [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] does.{{Refn|[[:File:Azmuth Knows the Reason For AF Diamondhead.png]]|group = DM}}
**Despite being destroyed, Chromastone's hologram appeared in ''[[The Secret of Chromastone]]''. However, selecting it transformed Ben into Diamondhead.<ref name="TSoC" />
*Chromastone is one of the four regular aliens to get a complete redesign in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]'''; the others being [[Shocksquatch]], [[Eatle]], and [[Swampfire]].
**Chromastone and Swampfire are the only two of these aliens to get redesigns mid-series (not counting [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]] getting clothes).
*Chromastone is one of the five aliens who escaped from the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original Omnitrix]]; the others being [[Ghostfreak]], [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]], [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]], and [[Spidermonkey (Classic)|Spidermonkey]].
**Chromastone is also one of four regular aliens to be temporarily destroyed and removed from the original Omnitrix/[[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]], the others being Way Big, Swampfire, and [[Feedback]].
*Chromastone is the final alien used on-screen in '''Ultimate Alien'''. Coincidentally, his hologram is also the first one shown on the reconfigured Omnitrix in '''Alien Force'''.<ref>''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''</ref>
**Chromastone is also the last alien to be used by Ben via the Ultimatrix.<ref name="TUEP2" />
*Chromastone's working name was Shard.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/23/Hero_Generation_Series_Bible.pdf Hero Generation Series Bible]|group = HG Bible|name = bible}}
*The first thing [[Dwayne McDuffie]] did when he pitched Chromastone was show the "secret" that was revealed in ''[[The Secret of Chromastone]]''.{{Refn|[[:File:Dwayne Had the Idea for The Secret of Chromastone Early On.png]]|group = DM}}
**It was Dwayne's idea to have Chromastone destroyed, for drama.{{Refn|group = CM|[[:File:Dwayne came up with Chromastone destruction.png]]}}
*Chromastone was initially not in ''[[Inside Man]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/24/Inside_Man_Script_Outline.pdf/revision/latest ''A Man Inside'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
*Chromastone was initially not meant to be destroyed during Season 2 of '''Alien Force'''. He was included in a few early script outlines for episodes, such as:
**''[[Singlehanded]]'': His role was taken by Diamondhead in the final version.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/3f/Singlehanded_Script_Outline.pdf ''Singlehanded'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
**''[[If All Else Fails]]'': He was used twice, with his role taken by [[Spidermonkey (Classic)|Spidermonkey]] and Diamondhead in the final version.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/c/c5/IAEF_Script_Outline.pdf ''If All Else Fails'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
*[[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] was originally supposed to turn into Chromastone in ''[[Inspector 13]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/f/f1/Inspector_13_Script_DRAFT-1.pdf ''Inspector 13'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = script}}
*Chromastone only appeared in two episodes of '''Omniverse''' because he didn't come up during story meetings,{{Refn|[[:File:Chromastone Didn't Come Up in OV.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Chromastone Didn't Come Up in OV 2.png]]|group = DJW}} did not have a proper redesign until ''A New Dawn'',{{Refn|[[:File:Chromastone Didn't Come Up in OV 3.png]]|group = DJW}} and had low toy sales during the previous shows' runs.{{Refn|[[:File:Psychobos Crab and Alien Absence.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Chromastone had concept art drawn by [[Glenn Wong]] and [[Eric Canete]],{{Refn|[[:File:Eric Canete Designed Alien X and Chromastone Concepts.png]]|group = EC}} whereas his final design was created by [[Chap Yaep]], with color styling by Chris Hooten.{{Refn|https://archive.is/Obhtg|group = GW|name = dk}}
**[[Glen Murakami]] gave Glenn Wong and Chap Yaep the DK eyewitness book on crystals to look at for inspiration.{{Refn|group = GW|name = dk}}
*Chromastone's design in ''[[A New Dawn]]'' is inspired by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gundam_(fictional_robot) Gundam].{{Refn|[[:File:Chromastone's New Design Inspiration.png]]|group = DJW}}
**The part of Chromastone face behind his eye was originally going to be black, just like in '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''.{{Refn|[[:File:Chromastone OV Concepts.png]]|group = DJW}}
**It was Derrick's favorite Chromastone design.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick's Favorite Chromastone Design.png]]|group = DJW}}

